    "explanation": "To both parties: this dispute goes to a human reviewer and no money moves. The SGD 4.00 cancellation fee is placed on hold — it is not collected from the rider and not refunded to them while review is pending.\n\nOn the merits, the driver's account is well supported. The trip record carries an 'arrived' event at 06:50:20 and shows the driver terminating the trip at 06:55:30 with reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW and no boarding event, and the GPS trace places his vehicle about 24 m from the pickup pin — inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius — stationary at 0 km/h for one continuous in-geofence hold running 06:50:00 to 06:55:30, i.e. 330 seconds against a 300-second minimum. POL-NS-01 limbs (a) to (d) are therefore all met. There is no false arrival marker (POL-NS-05: he was ~24 m out and stopped, far from the 300 m/15 km/h triggers), and no waiting-period shortfall (POL-NS-06), so nothing displaces the charge. The rider's device sat about 519 m from the pin, so POL-NS-04 does not assist them either. Left there, POL-NS-07 would pay the driver SGD 3.20 (80% of SGD 4.00), and the anti-farming guard is not tripped (1 no-show termination in 30 days, and 1/120 = 0.008 of completed trips, both below the thresholds).\n\nThat outcome cannot be issued, however. POL-NS-09(c) makes escalation mandatory where rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d together show 2 or more no-show disputes between the same rider and driver in the trailing 90 days. Both records show 2, and the rider's own claim describes this as 'another dispute with the same driver'. Escalation under POL-NS-09 is terminal and, per POL-GEN-03, replaces any monetary ruling — so the driver's compensation claim is accepted in substance but not paid out by the automated pipeline, and the rider's request is neither granted nor denied here.\n\nThe traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-09110-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) and carries no fact; it decides nothing, because the 330-second hold is a single unbroken interval and no accumulation under POL-NS-06(i) was needed.\n\nQuestion for the reviewer: whether this pair's repeated no-show disputes reflect a recurring genuine pickup problem or possible abuse on either side — a question a single trip's record cannot fairly settle."
